  concept: 'Authored objective: Verify the 18-layer training network.

    Authored
    requirement: Build 232 copper connections and 76 vias. Verify continuity in eight
    independent test domains.

    General teaching principle: PCB acceptance depends
    on the authored footprints, nets, layers, clearances and route constraints; visual
    appearance alone is insufficient.

    Only fresh, authoritative game evidence
    can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A multilayer road map helps visualize routing, but electrical continuity
    and constraints still require checks.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A visually connected trace is not proof of correct net connectivity
    or clearance.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Verify the 18-layer training network\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Verify the 18-layer training network\u2019, what result
    or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 113, perform the objective \u2018Verify the 18-layer training
    network\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against:
    Build 232 copper connections and 76 vias. Verify continuity in eight independent
    test domains.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does not
    grade your answer."
